          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong K3 surface
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+variety"} Calabi-Yau variety
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+variety"} Picard variety
            is zero-dimensional. In other words, it is a complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+surface"} algebraic surface
            with trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+bundle"} canonical bundle
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_X=\wedge^2\Omega_X\simeq \mathcal{O}_X
            ) and with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^1(X, \mathcal{O}_X)=0
          %p The term “K3” is
          %blockquote
            %p in honor of Kummer, Kähler, Kodaira, and the beautiful K2 mountain in Kashmir
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Weil79"}> Weil 79, p. 546
            )
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A cyclic cover of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℙ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^2
                branched over a curve of degree
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 6
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 6
            %li
              %p
                A nonsingular degree
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4
                hypersurface in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℙ
                          %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^3
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Fermat quartic
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Fermat+hypersurface"} ?
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi w
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi ℙ
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msup
                        %mi w
                        %mn 4
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 4
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mn 4
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi z
                        %mn 4
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{[w,x,y,z] \in \mathbb{P}^3 | w^4 + x^4 + y^4 + z^4 = 0\}
                (in fact every K3 surface over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
                to this example).
          %p
          #KummerSurface.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (Kummer surface)
              %br/
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+orbifold"} flat orbifold
              quotient of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-torus"} 4-torus
              (equipped with some
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
              on all four canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
              is the flat compact 4-dimensional orbifold known as a
              %em Kummer surface
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mn 4
                      %mo ⫽
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^4 \sslash \mathbb{Z}_2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
              (e.g.
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "Riemannian+orbifold#BettiolDerdzinskiPiccione18"} Bettiol, Derdzinski &amp; Piccione 2018, 5.5
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#TaorminaWendland15"} Taormina &amp; Wendland 2015, §1
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Dolgachev20"} Dolgachev 2020
            %div{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 30px"}
              %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
                %img{:src => "/nlab/files/KummerSurfaceProjections.png", :width => "500px"}/
                %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                  A sequence of 2d projections of the 4d Kummer surface, from
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#Dolgachev20"} Dolgachev 2020
            %p
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#compact_hyperkhler_structure Compact hyperkähler structure
          %p
            Over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3+surfaces"} K3 surfaces
            are all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} Kähler
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifold"} hyperkähler
          %p
            The only known examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+schemes+of+points"} Hilbert schemes of points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{[n+1]}
            (for
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            either
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-torus"} 4-torus
                (in which case the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
                is really the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕋
                          %mn 4
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕋
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{T}^4)^{[n]} \to \mathbb{T}^4
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "compact+hyperkähler+manifold#Beauville83"}> Beauville 83
            ) and two exceptional examples (
            %a{:href => "compact+hyperkähler+manifold#OGrady99"}> O’Grady 99
            ,
            %a{:href => "compact+hyperkähler+manifold#OGrady03"} O’Grady 03
            ), see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "compact+hyperkähler+manifold#Sawon04"} Sawon 04, Sec. 5.3
          %h3#homotopy Homotopy
          %ul
            %li
              All K3 surfaces are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected"} simply connected
          %h3#cohomology Cohomology
          #IntegralCohomology.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
              of a K3-surface
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℤ
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi n
                              %mo =
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi n
                              %mo =
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mn 22
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi n
                              %mo =
                              %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi n
                              %mo =
                              %mn 3
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℤ
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi n
                              %mo =
                              %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^n(X,\mathbb{Z})
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z} &amp;\vert&amp; n = 0
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\vert&amp; n = 1
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{Z}^{22} &amp;\vert&amp; n = 2
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\vert&amp; n = 3
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{Z} &amp;\vert&amp; n = 4
                    }
                    \\right.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BarthPetersVandenVen84"} Barth-Peters-Van den Ven 84, VIII Prop. 3.2
          #BettiNumbers.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Betti+numbers"} Betti numbers
                of a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
            %p
              The
              %span.newWikiWord
                Hodge diamond
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Hodge+diamond"} ?
              is completely determined (even in positive
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge-de+Rham+spectral+sequence"} Hodge-de Rham spectral sequence
              degenerates at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Betti+numbers"} Betti numbers
              are completely determined as
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 22
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1, 0, 22, 0, 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi h
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi h
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 0
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi h
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi h
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 0
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi h
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi h
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi h
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi h
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi h
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 20
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
